Subject: [PATCH 21/31] scsi: ncr53c710: complete negotiation message handshakes

After consuming the final negotiation reply byte, keep MSG IN visible until
the initiator releases ACK, then move to COMMAND. Otherwise NEXTSTEP 3.3
repeatedly enters SCSI error recovery instead of issuing its first command.

Accept an incoming MESSAGE REJECT without replying with another reject.
Negotiation remains declined; this does not introduce synchronous transfer
or guest-specific negotiation parameters. Regression coverage follows in
patch 22.

diff --git a/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c b/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c
--- a/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c
+++ b/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c
@@ -791,6 +791,7 @@
         case 0x04:
             ncr710_disconnect(s);
             break;
+        case 0x07:                       /* MESSAGE REJECT */
         case 0x08:                       /* NOP */
             ncr710_set_phase(s, PHASE_CMD);
             break;
@@ -1095,6 +1096,11 @@
                 }
                 if (insn & (1 << 6)) {
                     s->sbcl &= ~NCR710_SBCL_ACK;
+                    if ((s->sstat2 & PHASE_MASK) == PHASE_MI &&
+                        !s->msg_len &&
+                        s->msg_action == NCR710_MSG_ACTION_COMMAND) {
+                        ncr710_set_phase(s, PHASE_CMD);
+                    }
                 }
                 if (insn & (1 << 10)) {
                     s->carry = 0;
